# V-1 (docs/verve_v1_prereg.md): four races per launch. The menu part is gp_menu_full_press_dry_austria_grid_ai.plan
# (branch austria-plan) unchanged; after race 1, three restarts (@restart in tools/sandbox_shell.ps1: pause, Restart
# Session, confirm, the pre-race garage, pad a 700), each followed by its own @udpfinish. Every restart is a new UDP
# session uid; sandbox_shell passes the uids already ended to the next @udpfinish (--exclude-uids).
# Run by tools/v1_run.ps1 (one launch per call, that launch's verve.v1-l<LL> add-on switched on with -Addon).
# AUSTRIA (V-1, track rule): gp_menu_full_press_dry_hungary_grid_ai.plan with round 1 at the Red Bull Ring.
# AI (#134/#120): gp_menu_full_press_dry_hungary_grid.plan with a UDP-driven end instead of the results-screen wait.
# GRID (#131): gp_menu_full_press_dry_hungary.plan plus a Custom grid with the player last (Starting Grid add-on).
# HUNGARY (B-0018, #120): gp_menu_full_press_dry.plan with round 1 at the Hungaroring.
# DRY-LOCKED (#118): gp_menu_full_press.plan plus Quick Weather = Clear (Dry), found by the H-dry discovery on build
# 26566308 (2026-11-16). The runner's weather_check --locked then requires weather 0 and a dry forecast throughout.
# A full menu Grand Prix for behaviour batches (#71): as gp_menu_race.plan, at AI difficulty 100, run to the results
# screen. Tools/b0014_check.py reads the difficulty back from UDP, and any race not at 100 is invalid.
wait screen=splash 180
pad ls 15000
pad ls
pad ls 2000
pad ls
home
@sleep 3
@raw {"seq":0,"cmd":"route","args":{"route":"f1_world"},"timeout_ms":60000}
@sleep 5
@expect fe_f1_world
@raw {"seq":0,"cmd":"route","args":{"route":"play"},"timeout_ms":60000}
@sleep 6
@expect f1_world_activity_container
# the Grand Prix card
pad a 250
@sleep 6
# the season: one right is F1 2025
pad right 250
@sleep 3
pad a 250
@sleep 6
@expect solo_container
# round 1's track: ten right from Australia is Austria (Red Bull Ring, UDP track id 17; seen on screen in the
# H-dry discovery, 26566308). V-1 runs at Austria by the track rule (net held passes per race-minute 3.8x Hungary).
pad right 200
pad right 200
pad right 200
pad right 200
pad right 200
pad right 200
pad right 200
pad right 200
pad right 200
pad right 200
@sleep 2
pad a 250
@sleep 7
@expect solo_container
# team: four right from McLaren is Aston Martin. Then the driver: Stroll is the default
pad right 200
pad right 200
pad right 200
pad right 200
@sleep 2
pad a 250
@sleep 7
@expect solo_container
pad a 250
@sleep 7
@expect settings_container
# Difficulty 100: from Start Event, right then down is the Difficulty tile. Holding right reaches the cap of 110 from
# any start, and ten presses left from there is exactly 100. Then back to the hub (Difficulty selected).
pad right 250
@sleep 2
pad down 250
@sleep 2
pad a 250
@sleep 4
pad right 6000
@sleep 2
pad left 200
pad left 200
pad left 200
pad left 200
pad left 200
pad left 200
pad left 200
pad left 200
pad left 200
pad left 200
@sleep 2
pad b 250
@sleep 4
# #131 workaround grid (msyeett.starting-grid 0.1.4, enabled in verve-test): down from Difficulty is Weekend Structure
# (Qualifying Format Off, Starting Grid Realistic). Five down is Grid Editor; opening it makes Starting Grid Custom.
# The player (Stroll) starts at P1 with the cursor on him; X moves him down one, 19 presses put him 20th (last)
# and every AI car moves up one in the game's order. B asks Confirm Changes (A), B again is the hub on Weekend
# Structure, and up is Difficulty again for the weather steps. Found by runs/2026-11-16-H-grid-discovery.
pad down 250
@sleep 2
pad a 250
@sleep 4
pad down 200
@sleep 1
pad down 200
@sleep 1
pad down 200
@sleep 1
pad down 200
@sleep 1
pad down 200
@sleep 1
@sleep 1
pad a 250
@sleep 4
pad x 250
@sleep 1
pad x 250
@sleep 1
pad x 250
@sleep 1
pad x 250
@sleep 1
pad x 250
@sleep 1
pad x 250
@sleep 1
pad x 250
@sleep 1
pad x 250
@sleep 1
pad x 250
@sleep 1
pad x 250
@sleep 1
pad x 250
@sleep 1
pad x 250
@sleep 1
pad x 250
@sleep 1
pad x 250
@sleep 1
pad x 250
@sleep 1
pad x 250
@sleep 1
pad x 250
@sleep 1
pad x 250
@sleep 1
pad x 250
@sleep 1
@sleep 2
pad b 250
@sleep 4
# Confirm Changes
pad a 250
@sleep 4
pad b 250
@sleep 4
pad up 250
@sleep 2
# #118 weather lock: up then right from Difficulty is the Weather and Time of Day tile. Its first row, Quick Weather,
# starts at Dynamic (random weather); one press right is Clear (Dry), which holds for the whole weekend.
pad up 250
@sleep 2
pad right 250
@sleep 2
pad a 250
@sleep 4
pad right 250
@sleep 3
# back to the hub (Weather selected), then two left is Start Event
pad b 250
@sleep 4
pad left 250
@sleep 2
pad left 250
@sleep 3
# back on the hub, Start Event selected
pad a 250
@sleep 8
# one press inside the grid rundown, before lights out (about 108 s into the session), for #65
@sleep 125
# only press inside the rundown: on the grid, this press would fire Start Race. All 3 test runs read this state
@expect \|hud\|#fe9b028c\|
pad a 250
@sleep 4
status
wait screen=garage_monitor_container 300
@sleep 8
@expect garage_monitor_container
pad a 700
@sleep 2
@raw {"seq":0,"cmd":"ai_drives_player","args":{"on":true},"timeout_ms":30000}
@sleep 2
@raw {"seq":0,"cmd":"ai_drives_player","args":{"on":true},"timeout_ms":30000}
# AI-only (spectator garage start, #134): the player car is parked in the garage and never finishes, so there is no
# results screen. Quit when every AI car is done by UDP LapData, at most the leader's finish + 150 s (#134 ruling 4).
@udpfinish 900 150
# race 2: restart from the pause menu (same grid), then the same UDP-driven end
@restart
@udpfinish 900 150
# race 3: restart from the pause menu (same grid), then the same UDP-driven end
@restart
@udpfinish 900 150
# race 4: restart from the pause menu (same grid), then the same UDP-driven end
@restart
@udpfinish 900 150
status
